indications_limitations:
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;p&gt; A.  Manipulation of the Rib Cage&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;

&lt;p&gt; Manual manipulation of the rib cage contributes to the treatment of respiratory conditions such as bronchitis, emphysema, and asthma as part of a regimen which includes other elements of therapy, and is covered only under such circumstances.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;&lt;p&gt; B.  Manipulation of the Head&lt;&sol;p&gt;&lt;&sol;strong&gt;

&lt;p&gt; Manipulation of the occipitocervical or temporomandibular regions of the head when indicated for conditions affecting those portions of the head and neck is a covered service.&lt;&sol;p&gt;
